    "display_name": "Dinosaurs",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Build a classifier to determine if a dinosaur description is of an herbivore or a carnivore.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/f2fe3bc55835407430ff5a8e0708d541-tyrannosaurus.png",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "import csv\n\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n\nfrom helpers import tokenize, visualize_model\n\n\ndef get_features(text):\n  # TODO: Compute bag of words features\n  counts = {}\n  return counts\n\n\n# Read data\nf = open(\"dinosaurs.csv\")\ndata = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# Compute features and labels for data\nall_features = [get_features(row[\"text\"]) for row in data]\noutputs = [row[\"label\"] for row in data]\n\n\n# Get all unique words in dataset\nvocabulary = []\nfor features in all_features:\n  for word in features:\n    if word not in vocabulary:\n      vocabulary.append(word)\nvocabulary.sort()\n\n# For each input, compute feature values for all words in vocabulary\ninputs = []\nfor features in all_features:\n  vector = []\n  for word in vocabulary:\n    if word in features:\n      vector.append(features[word])\n    else:\n      vector.append(0)\n  inputs.append(vector)\n\n# Split data into training and testing sets\ntrain_inputs, test_inputs, train_outputs, test_outputs = train_test_split(\n  inputs, outputs, test_size=0.25\n)\n\n# Train model\nmodel = DecisionTreeClassifier()\nmodel.fit(train_inputs, train_outputs)\n\n# Visualize decision tree\nvisualize_model(model, vocabulary)\n\n# Test model\nmodel_score = model.score(test_inputs, test_outputs)\nprint(\"Model score on test data:\", model_score)\n\nf.close()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "dinosaurs.csv",
          "contents": "text,label\n\"It stripped leaves from high branches with a long neck and blunt flat teeth.\",herbivore\n\"Its sharp serrated teeth cut through the flesh and bone of its prey.\",carnivore\n\"Flat grinding teeth let it chew tough ferns and other low plants all day.\",herbivore\n\"This hunter caught fish in the shallows with a narrow snout of sharp teeth.\",carnivore\n\"Bony plates along its back may have released heat while it fed on low plants.\",herbivore\n\"A curved claw on each foot pinned its prey while the jaws closed.\",carnivore\n\"It moved in herds, and trackways show the young walking at the center of the herd.\",herbivore\n\"Its jaws delivered the strongest bite of any hunter that ever walked on land.\",carnivore\n\"A heavy club on its tail helped it fight off the hunters that chased the herd.\",herbivore\n\"Crushed bone in its droppings shows this hunter swallowed prey in large pieces.\",carnivore\n\"A wide flat beak let it crop low plants and leaves close to the ground.\",herbivore\n\"Forward facing eyes gave this hunter the depth perception it needed to catch prey.\",carnivore\n\"Stones in its stomach helped grind the tough plants it swallowed without chewing.\",herbivore\n\"It scavenged the meat of dead animals as often as it hunted living prey.\",carnivore\n\"Its horns and broad frill were used for display in the herd as much as defense.\",herbivore\n\"Healed bite marks on rival skulls show these hunters fought each other over meat.\",carnivore\n\"It weighed as much as ten elephants and spent the whole day eating plants.\",herbivore\n\"Long light legs suggest this hunter chased fast prey instead of waiting in ambush.\",carnivore\n\"Hundreds of packed flat teeth formed a surface for shredding tough fibrous plants.\",herbivore\n\"Its jaws held sixty sharp teeth, and it replaced them throughout its life.\",carnivore\n\"A crest on its duck billed skull carried calls across the feeding herd.\",herbivore\n\"Sharp curved claws are preserved on both the hands and the feet of this hunter.\",carnivore\n\"It reared onto its hind legs to reach leaves that other plant eaters could not.\",herbivore\n\"Several of these hunters at one site suggest they chased prey in packs.\",carnivore\n\"Its armored back and short legs made it slow but hard for any hunter to kill.\",herbivore\n\"Its teeth were thin and blade like, better for slicing meat than crushing bone.\",carnivore\n\"Nests found together show that adults returned to feed the young of the herd.\",herbivore\n\"This hunter took the young and the injured from the edges of passing herds.\",carnivore\n\"A long heavy tail balanced its neck as it swept its head across the plants.\",herbivore\n\"Air pockets kept its skull light without weakening the bite of its jaws.\",carnivore\n\"It raked conifer needles from branches with peg shaped teeth and swallowed them whole.\",herbivore\n\"Long arms with three hooked claws held the prey while its teeth went to work.\",carnivore\n\"The thick dome of its skull was used for shoving matches within the herd.\",herbivore\n\"A stiff tail worked as a counterweight during the fast turns of a chase.\",carnivore\n\"Rings in its bones show it took twenty years of eating plants to reach full size.\",herbivore\n\"Puncture wounds in a plant eating herd's hip match the spacing of this hunter's teeth.\",carnivore\n\"Wear on its jaw shows the side to side chewing motion suited to grinding plants.\",herbivore\n\"It grew fast, adding two kilograms a day on a diet of meat.\",carnivore\n\"It stood four meters at the shoulder and fed on shrubs and low leaves.\",herbivore\n\"Feathers on its arms were for display, not flight, in this fast hunter.\",carnivore\n\"Trackways record a herd of dozens moving together across an open floodplain.\",herbivore\n\"Its narrow snout reached into cracks to pull out smaller prey.\",carnivore\n\"Spines along its shoulders made it awkward for a hunter to bring the animal down.\",herbivore\n\"Trackways show this hunter following a herd along the same path for a kilometer.\",carnivore\n\"Its small head carried no cutting teeth at all, only pegs for raking leaves.\",herbivore\n\"Its claws stayed off the ground as it walked, which kept them sharp for the hunt.\",carnivore\n\"It fed on lower branches than its larger relatives, which reduced competition in the herd.\",herbivore\n\"Large eye sockets suggest this hunter tracked its prey at night.\",carnivore\n\"Droppings at the site are packed with crushed wood and conifer leaves.\",herbivore\n\"Marks on fossil bone show it stripped meat with a backward pull of its jaws.\",carnivore\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "helpers.py",
          "contents": "import re\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n  return re.findall(r\"\\w+\", text.lower())\n\n\ndef visualize_model(model, feature_names=None, decimals=2):\n  \"\"\"Pretty-print the questions a fitted DecisionTreeClassifier asks.\"\"\"\n  tree = model.tree_\n\n  if feature_names is None:\n    n = getattr(model, \"n_features_in_\", None) or tree.n_features\n    feature_names = [\"feature_\" + str(i) for i in range(n)]\n\n  TEE, ELBOW, BAR, ARROW = \"├─\", \"└─\", \"│\", \"→\"\n  LABELS = (\"YES\", \"NO \")\n  STEM = len(TEE) + 1 + len(LABELS[0]) + 1 + len(ARROW) + 1\n\n  def number(x):\n    text = \"{:.{}f}\".format(x, decimals)\n    return text.rstrip(\"0\").rstrip(\".\") if \".\" in text else text\n\n  def class_counts(node):\n    raw = list(tree.value[node][0])\n    total = tree.n_node_samples[node]\n    if abs(sum(raw) - total) > 1e-6:  # sklearn >= 1.4 stores proportions\n      raw = [p * total for p in raw]\n    return [int(round(c)) for c in raw], total\n\n  def is_leaf(node):\n    return tree.children_left[node] == -1\n\n  def describe_leaf(node):\n    counts, total = class_counts(node)\n    best = max(range(len(counts)), key=lambda i: counts[i])\n    answer = str(model.classes_[best])\n    if counts[best] == total:\n      plural = \"\" if total == 1 else \"s\"\n      return \"{}  ({} example{})\".format(answer, total, plural)\n    order = sorted(range(len(counts)), key=lambda i: -counts[i])\n    mix = \", \".join(\n      \"{} {}\".format(counts[i], model.classes_[i]) for i in order if counts[i] > 0\n    )\n    return \"{}  ({})\".format(answer, mix)\n\n  def question(node):\n    return \"Is {} <= {}?\".format(\n      feature_names[tree.feature[node]],\n      number(float(tree.threshold[node])),\n    )\n\n  def describe(node):\n    return describe_leaf(node) if is_leaf(node) else question(node)\n\n  def walk(node, prefix):\n    children = (tree.children_left[node], tree.children_right[node])\n    for i, child in enumerate(children):\n      last = i == len(children) - 1\n      connector = ELBOW if last else TEE\n      print(\n        \"{}{} {} {} {}\".format(\n          prefix, connector, LABELS[i], ARROW, describe(child)\n        )\n      )\n      if not is_leaf(child):\n        spacer = \" \" if last else BAR\n        walk(child, prefix + spacer + \" \" * (STEM - len(spacer)))\n\n  print(describe(0))\n  if not is_leaf(0):\n    walk(0, \"\")",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false,
          "type": "support"
        }
      },
